senses.gloss:
vidhā́na, n. a dis-position, ordering, ordinance;
 vidhānatas, according to (established)
ordinance. [√1dhā + vi, 1150.]

vidhú, a. lonely (of the moon that
wanders alone among the star-hosts);
as m. moon. [prob. fr. √2vidh, 1178.]

vidhura, a.
 —1. alone, bereft;
 —2. suffering
lack, miserable;
 —3. disagreeable;
as n. trouble. [prob. fr. √2vidh, through
the intermediate vidhu, 1188f.]
